Captain Sloan,

I'm sending this to you as a courtesy.

You redirected me to FOIA and I pursued it. I choose not to file with the F=
orestry out of respect for our District Ranger and for the Forest Service w=
e both serve.

My focus, as it has always been, is on accountability at the state level. T=
hey expelled me for protected speech and put it in writing. They did that b=
ecause I documented abuse I experienced as a volunteer with them. What your=
 officer opened at that gate was retaliation delivered on the one year anni=
versary of that experience. Did you know that?

I don't know how to reconcile that anymore than you probably do. It happene=
d. It's part of the record. And I'm doing my best to focus on the ones who =
truly harmed me. And I do understand your silence around my questions, but =
you are letting an impossible characterization stand: that Oregon State Pol=
ice were here because you wanted them here. How can that possibly be true? =
Who gave them my birthdate and the location where I live? What does "for th=
e Forest Service" mean?

I cannot separate this from the accountability I am seeking from the State =
of Oregon -- who it was that deliberately used police to intimidate me, how=
 they can justify a letter that cites only my protected speech as cause for=
 anything -- because your officer participated, and to protect him, you can=
't protect me, even though duty compels it.

I am willing to indemnify your entire institution for this act, in writing,=
 if you acknowledge it honestly. I only care that the record is accurate, a=
nd the record shows you were used as much as anyone. They tried to drive a =
wedge into a relationship that was not theirs to influence. Where do you st=
and in this?

Robert Samuel White


