To the Public Records Advocate / Attorney General's Office:

I petition the Attorney General for a Public Records Order under ORS 192.41=
1, ORS 192.324(6), and ORS 192.407. The public body is the Oregon State Pol=
ice, Central Records Section. The request is PR27478, submitted April 3, 20=
26, concerning OSP CAD event SP26097765.

In brief: OSP issued a "no records" determination on April 3, 2026. Ten day=
s later a responsive CAD record was printed inside its Central Records Sect=
ion; it was produced to me on July 14, 2026 =97 in full, with no exemption =
claimed and no fee charged =97 after being conditioned for three months on =
a $12.50 payment and a mailed paper form. One hundred and ten days after th=
e request, five of the requested categories remain without any disposition,=
 no exemption has been cited for anything, the search has never been descri=
bed, the fee waiver has never been ruled on, and the litigation preservatio=
n notice I served on April 2, 2026 has never been acknowledged.

The attached petition sets out the record in full and states the relief req=
uested. The exhibits (1=9625) are the complete correspondence and the produ=
ced record, in a single indexed and page-labeled PDF; the exhibit index app=
ears in Section VII of the petition. I am not asking the Attorney General t=
o make any finding about the underlying event =97 only to require Oregon St=
ate Police to respond to a public records request as the statute requires.

I can provide any exhibit as a separate file on request.

Respectfully,

